  "benchmark": "crates/penelope-sqlite/benches/machine_backpressure.rs",
  "scope": "Authorized public machine commits submitted in one burst while an independent SQLite connection holds BEGIN IMMEDIATE. Queue capacities 1/8, burst sizes 32/128; one shared head, distinct event identities and the real shared bounded worker.",
  "reuse": "Existing journal integration model/codec/preparation/async driver and durable measurement runner. No new evaluator, worker or queue implementation. Legacy runner default and fixtures preserved.",
