    "debug": "All dimensions/invariants, 1 warmup and 3 measured smoke rounds; the actual measurement helper refuses these results.",
    "storage": "NVMe Btrfs, existing SQLite WAL/FULL configuration and busy timeout, CPU4. Independent writer lock released immediately after submitting the burst; no sleeps or private queue access."
  },
  "oracle": "Each burst accepts between 1 and capacity+1 requests, refuses every other request as Capacity during its first poll, then produces exactly one Committed receipt and admitted-1 StaleHead results after lock release. Winner identity, exact retry, full retained payload/intent, snapshot state/revision, final event/intent counts and SQLite integrity checked. Each profile ends with 109 events/intents including warmup.",
  "timing": "Individual call construction + first poll for refusal and accepted admission. Future destruction after a ready refusal is outside timing. Accepted completion includes deliberate writer-lock gating, burst submission and sequential caller draining. These are separate populations. Raw samples are chronological pooled per-call values; raw per-round counts give population sizes. Model preparation and post-call assertions are untimed. No timer subtraction or outlier removal.",
