  "assessment": [
    "All measured bounds, receipts, histories, raw counts/ranks and expected debug-mode refusal passed. Current refusal medians were 60 ns; pooled p99 ranged 140-260 ns across profiles/runs. These tiny intervals include timer/allocator/codegen effects and clock quantization; they are not latency guarantees.",
    "Queue occupancy can be capacity or capacity+1 depending on worker scheduling; the active job is separate from the bounded channel. The fixture tolerates this real scheduling variation without widening configured limits.",
    "Capacity is a broader public error class. Here known valid requests, fixed bounds and the controlled writer gate identify queue pressure. Other Capacity errors may represent payload/history/storage limits.",
    "The native pipeline remains a separate real execution measurement. This profile measures machine-store queue backpressure, not native process max_live saturation, task scheduler throughput or external effect CPU.",
    "The candidate API immediately refuses excess valid requests and preserves one authoritative transition. Gated accepted-completion observations are not steady-state latency or a service-capacity estimate. No performance waiver, security downgrade or weakened check.",
    "Whole-process RSS is retained by the runner; allocations/stack and per-operation disk writes are not measured. CPU pinning does not isolate frequency/system load; the long chaos campaign runs on CPUs8-15. Final qualification and legacy performance findings remain open."
  ],
